for what it's worth ... "winning" games are commonly characterized
by the trait that you are now a level 8 (or so) character emerging
for the first time on dungeon level 10 with poison resistance,
invisibility or speed, a named weapon with bonuses (there's always
Sting, Orcrist and Excalibur) and an AC rating better than -5.
under these conditions you can survive on dungeon levels 10-20
(virtually) forever which you'll then want to do because the mere
passage of time has a way of enhancing your survival odds since
you're bound to discover some things which can give you an advantage.
there's really no need to push the game after this ...

of course, this picture was painted in the broadest of strokes
but it should help.

